1	/**
2	 * The CVA round of the `angular-tiny-translator-v0-12-0` cell: the era
3	 * call-site semantics of `ControlValueAccessor.setDisabledState`, restored.
4	 *
5	 * u19h measured a silent typed-data loss on the migrated lane and u19i
6	 * attributed it: Angular 16's `setUpControl` calls `setDisabledState` on every
7	 * accessor as it attaches, this application's accessor rebuilds the very
8	 * `FormGroup` its own debounced subscription is watching, and the edit the user
9	 * types therefore reaches nothing. Angular 5 called the method only for a
10	 * control that was already disabled, so on the era cell the body never ran.
11	 *
12	 * The repair is the vendor's own switch, provided rather than written:
13	 * `CALL_SET_DISABLED_STATE` as `'whenDisabledForLegacyCode'`. This driver reads
14	 * the applied tree's own TypeScript modules and hands them to
15	 * `@versionless/angular`. It decides which tree is rewritten and nothing else —
16	 * whether an accessor is one the era guard was hiding is read out of the
17	 * application's own `setDisabledState` bodies, and where the provider goes is
18	 * read out of the module that bootstraps.
